WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
[MUSIC]

00:00:14.895 --> 00:00:16.720
Hi, everyone, my name is Dr.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.444
Madhu Shetti, I'm a board
certified radiation oncologist,

00:00:20.444 --> 00:00:24.469
practicing in the San Francisco East Bay
prior to coming to the GSB.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:31.226
When I have been taking care of patients,
I have noticed that many of my patients

00:00:31.226 --> 00:00:35.140
experienced many of the problems
that I experienced growing up.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.467
My patients had language barriers,
transportation barriers,

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:39.560
cultural barriers.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:44.425
And oftentimes, when they would seek care,
they were afraid that they were not going

00:00:44.425 --> 00:00:49.240
to get the best care, or they were not
going to be treated as well as others.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:49.953
My team and

00:00:49.953 --> 00:00:55.421
I strove to make sure that every patient
walking in our door felt respected, and we

00:00:55.421 --> 00:01:00.990
gave them the best possible care with them
as a partner in every step of the process.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:06.954
Unfortunately, the financial realities
of our hospital system were such

00:01:06.954 --> 00:01:09.670
that we ended up closing the hospital, and

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:13.380
our community really is
the one who felt the loss.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.940
I came to GSB with the intention of
gaining formal business skills so

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:23.149
that I could help other communities
keep their health care systems in place.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:27.466
So that individual could get good high
quality care close to home with all

00:01:27.466 --> 00:01:31.996
the support that they already have built
in during a very challenging time in

00:01:31.996 --> 00:01:33.530
their life.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.941
And as I've been at GSB taking
classes from all disciplines,

00:01:36.941 --> 00:01:40.080
I started to take
entrepreneurship classes.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.470
And then I became
an accidental entrepreneur.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:49.760
One of the big challenges that I've seen
for patients undergoing radiation or

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:53.870
chemotherapy is that they
developed significant hair loss.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:58.233
Their face can develop significant ashy or
pale dry looks, and

00:01:58.233 --> 00:02:00.712
their fingernails can turn black.

00:02:00.712 --> 00:02:05.163
And their fingers and toes can develop
severe numbness, tingling sensations,

00:02:05.163 --> 00:02:07.000
and swelling.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:11.334
Until you experience some of these
symptoms, one does not realize how much it

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:15.670
impacts our life and
particularly our emotional well being.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:19.726
What we don't talk about is the other
symptoms that you just can't see

00:02:19.726 --> 00:02:21.524
because they're covered up.

00:02:21.524 --> 00:02:25.974
So many of my patients who are undergoing
radiation to the breast will have

00:02:25.974 --> 00:02:30.137
significant redness, pinkness,
it's a peeling, a burning, and

00:02:30.137 --> 00:02:31.666
a weeping of the tissue.

00:02:31.666 --> 00:02:36.784
Oftentimes, it can feel like the worst
sunburn they've ever had in life.

00:02:36.784 --> 00:02:40.699
Some of my patients have been so
devastated in the process, both physically

00:02:40.699 --> 00:02:46.020
and emotionally of their cancer diagnosis,
that they have actually become suicidal.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:50.693
And that's where it becomes so important
to have a team taking care of one to give

00:02:50.693 --> 00:02:55.600
you all the support, both physically and
emotionally, to get through that time.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:00.190
As I researched different
products to help my patients,

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:03.400
I never could find
anything I really liked.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.929
Even products that are labeled as organic,
natural, or

00:03:06.929 --> 00:03:12.380
clean oftentimes have ingredients that can
be harmful to patients during the process.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.407
And it can be that the ingredient
can trigger a migraine or nausea.

00:03:17.407 --> 00:03:21.065
Or it could be that the ingredients
interact at the skin, and

00:03:21.065 --> 00:03:24.164
can actually cause worsening
of skin irritation.

00:03:24.164 --> 00:03:28.692
And in the very worst case, it can
actually block some of the pathways for

00:03:28.692 --> 00:03:30.103
the chemoradiation,

00:03:30.103 --> 00:03:34.276
which will make it ultimately
ineffective at curing your cancer.

00:03:34.276 --> 00:03:39.196
So it's very important that patients be
able to get the correct information about

00:03:39.196 --> 00:03:44.488
the products that they're spending so much
time and money to purchase and understand.

00:03:44.488 --> 00:03:48.460
Is it a product that will help them or
is it a product that will hurt them?

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:53.599
And that led to the process of
starting my company Bomb Your Skin.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:58.482
So that I could make sure we could
get high quality products to

00:03:58.482 --> 00:04:01.660
patients as they were on this journey.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:06.585
I could not have done this
process without the support of my

00:04:06.585 --> 00:04:11.219
classmates, from my teachers,
and from GSB alumni.

00:04:11.219 --> 00:04:16.136
Who have given me feedback on
what I could do, context for

00:04:16.136 --> 00:04:22.580
how I could execute faster, or the
resources of how do I launch a company?

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:24.210
How do I hire individuals?

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:27.805
Every step of that journey
requires special skills.

00:04:27.805 --> 00:04:32.025
And the entire GSB community
has supported my vision, and

00:04:32.025 --> 00:04:35.480
helped me to be able to
execute in that process.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:40.421
I'm eternally grateful for everything
each member of the GSB community

00:04:40.421 --> 00:04:45.040
has done to help me in the process
to fulfill my mission.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:49.100
So I urge you to think about GSB
in your future career plans.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:53.220
If you're an entrepreneur,
this is an awesome place to be.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:58.554
And if you're not an entrepreneurial,
and you wanted to go into other avenues,

00:04:58.554 --> 00:05:03.114
you very well might become
an accidental entrepreneur like myself.

00:05:03.114 --> 00:05:05.079
Thank you so much.

00:05:05.079 --> 00:05:05.579
[MUSIC]

